WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.675
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.675 --> 00:03.344
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION AND
SHAMEFUL ACTS ARE NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:03.344 --> 00:04.970
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:10.267 --> 00:13.896
Let's ride out into
the highway of our youth

00:13.896 --> 00:16.899
Right now is always
the best of the season

00:17.107 --> 00:20.569
Get high on hope,
as we adults keep winning

00:20.653 --> 00:24.114
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

00:24.114 --> 00:27.409
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

00:27.451 --> 00:29.537
Ever Endless

00:30.746 --> 00:32.414
Ever Endless

00:34.166 --> 00:35.709
Ever Endless

00:37.586 --> 00:38.963
Ever Endless

00:39.630 --> 00:44.426
Mon-Tues-Weds-Thurs-Fri,
my life knows no variety

00:44.426 --> 00:45.845
Ever Endless

00:46.262 --> 00:51.058
Sat-Sun, wake up in the afternoon
with only my smartphone to surf

00:51.058 --> 00:52.643
Ever Endless

00:52.643 --> 00:54.061
All my limbs' been giving in

00:54.061 --> 00:55.896
Kalbi's a burden like my lumber spine

00:55.896 --> 00:57.481
Doing family service with irises dim

00:57.481 --> 00:59.108
But you know that I'll go all the way

00:59.525 --> 01:02.695
Glitter, shimmer,
the light's shining

01:02.987 --> 01:06.532
Let's give it one more chance

01:06.532 --> 01:09.994
Let's ride out into
the highway of our youth

01:10.202 --> 01:12.997
Right now is always
the best of the season

01:13.205 --> 01:16.834
Get high on hope,
as we adults keep winning

01:16.834 --> 01:19.837
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

01:20.087 --> 01:22.214
Youth is when you never...

01:22.214 --> 01:23.716
stop chasing your own values

01:23.716 --> 01:25.384
Our youth's eternal

01:25.384 --> 01:26.969
the color never fades with age

01:26.969 --> 01:28.846
Youth is when you keep...

01:28.846 --> 01:30.389
getting lost along the way

01:30.389 --> 01:33.934
Youth is Forever

01:46.488 --> 01:47.823
Let's go!

01:47.823 --> 01:49.450
One chance...

01:49.450 --> 01:53.245
- To score!
- To score!

01:56.957 --> 01:58.751
Hey, don't say "one chance."

01:58.751 --> 02:00.711
I'd love two or three.

02:00.711 --> 02:02.004
That's true.

02:03.297 --> 02:05.591
Alright, we get it.

02:05.591 --> 02:07.218
For now, how about you get out?

02:07.218 --> 02:08.469
NO ENTRY

02:08.719 --> 02:10.387
So, what do we do now?

02:10.387 --> 02:12.348
Climbing the wall didn't work.

02:12.348 --> 02:15.518
We have no choice but to
break through the front.

02:16.685 --> 02:19.647
I don't think we can
brute force our way in.

02:21.023 --> 02:22.566
What about digging a tunnel?

02:22.858 --> 02:25.277
Find a crack in the wall or something?

02:25.528 --> 02:26.529
Hold on!

02:26.529 --> 02:27.905
There's no need for that.

02:27.905 --> 02:28.948
Hmm?

02:28.948 --> 02:30.866
- We've got a plan.
- We've got a plan.

02:30.866 --> 02:31.867
Oho.

02:32.034 --> 02:34.203
Our method is incredibly simple.

02:34.537 --> 02:36.830
Hold your head high and walk through.

02:38.040 --> 02:40.960
Look, it's hard to stop someone
with a lot of confidence, right?

02:41.210 --> 02:44.463
We'll make them think we just
overlooked the ticket checking.

02:44.871 --> 02:45.664
I see.

02:45.798 --> 02:48.217
No matter how you look at it,
isn't that too sloppy?

02:48.717 --> 02:50.427
Don't worry, Mitarai.

02:50.761 --> 02:52.805
This plan has a backup.

02:56.684 --> 02:58.936
PRETENDING NOT TO HEAR
BECAUSE OF HIS HEADPHONES

03:01.313 --> 03:03.566
PRETENDING TO HAVE MIXED UP HIS TICKETS

03:05.943 --> 03:08.195
PRETENDING TO BE AN OUMI STUDENT

03:10.531 --> 03:12.825
PRETENDING TO BE
AN ELEMENTARY SCHOOL STUDENT

03:15.077 --> 03:17.496
There's a lot of things I wanna say.

03:17.496 --> 03:20.291
But why are you guys looking down on us?

03:20.291 --> 03:21.375
We would never.

03:21.375 --> 03:22.918
We're honestly trying our best.

03:23.544 --> 03:25.004
Oh my god!

03:25.004 --> 03:26.922
Did Japan's education go this bad?

03:27.214 --> 03:28.507
Anyway,

03:28.507 --> 03:30.384
it's hopeless
no matter how much you try.

03:30.384 --> 03:31.594
Go home quietly!

03:32.094 --> 03:33.512
We'll go home quietly...

03:33.512 --> 03:35.848
so could you give us
directions to the station?

03:35.848 --> 03:36.557
Huh?

03:36.557 --> 03:37.558
Now's the time! Go!

03:42.354 --> 03:43.397
Hold it!

03:45.024 --> 03:46.066
That was close.

03:46.066 --> 03:47.484
We can't let our guard down.

03:47.735 --> 03:48.861
Hmph, you fools.

03:48.861 --> 03:49.820
You fell for it.

03:50.779 --> 03:52.448
They were just baits.

03:52.448 --> 03:53.657
What!?

03:53.908 --> 03:55.993
We won't let you!

03:57.328 --> 03:58.537
Let go!

03:58.537 --> 04:00.748
I'm not letting go!

04:00.748 --> 04:03.709
I don't care
if you say it's pointless.

04:03.876 --> 04:06.754
In the name of our friendship...

04:06.921 --> 04:10.508
we won't let you go on your own!

04:10.508 --> 04:11.717
NO ENTRY

04:11.717 --> 04:14.011
Why would you grab our legs?

04:14.011 --> 04:16.138
What's the point in getting in our way?

04:16.138 --> 04:17.848
Shut up, you damn traitors!

04:17.848 --> 04:20.309
You didn't say anything
about us being bait!

04:20.309 --> 04:21.227
You bastard!

04:21.644 --> 04:23.729
We shouldn't really say anything...

04:23.729 --> 04:26.398
but shouldn't you even
try to work together?

04:27.399 --> 04:30.027
Damn! We were just one step away!

04:30.236 --> 04:31.904
Were we too complacent?

04:31.904 --> 04:33.447
You call that one step away?

04:33.447 --> 04:35.491
Just how long is your stride?

04:35.699 --> 04:38.410
We don't have time
to sit around leisurely.

04:38.410 --> 04:41.664
Those girls seem like they'd draw
attentions without makeup.

04:41.664 --> 04:42.790
That's right!

04:42.998 --> 04:45.000
UGLY! - ATTRACTIVE!Right now, Chisa isn't using any makeup.

04:45.000 --> 04:46.210
Which means

04:46.210 --> 04:48.087
the odds that she gets hit on...

04:48.087 --> 04:51.090
Iori-kun...

04:51.757 --> 04:53.717
Since it's come to this,
let's forge a ticket!

04:53.717 --> 04:55.719
No, let's dress up like professors!

04:55.719 --> 04:56.887
Pretend to be injured!

04:56.887 --> 04:58.556
Parachute in from the sky!

04:58.806 --> 05:00.975
Huh? What are you doing, Iori?

05:01.517 --> 05:02.685
OUMI FESTIVAL STAFF

05:06.230 --> 05:08.148
Hey, Kitahara, who's this beautiful lady?

05:08.148 --> 05:09.108
Your acquaintance?

05:09.108 --> 05:10.401
Introduce us!

05:10.401 --> 05:11.318
That's your friend?

05:11.318 --> 05:13.195
Depends.

05:13.779 --> 05:14.864
Give it up, you guys.

05:14.864 --> 05:17.616
This one's way out of your league.

05:18.117 --> 05:18.868
Huh?

05:19.159 --> 05:21.078
It's true that she's super beautiful.

05:21.078 --> 05:23.038
Are her standards that high?

05:23.038 --> 05:24.540
They're not exactly high...

05:26.166 --> 05:27.418
they're beyond help.

05:28.669 --> 05:29.795
Beyond help!?

05:29.795 --> 05:31.297
What's that supposed to mean?

05:31.797 --> 05:34.049
- So, what are you doing?
- Beyond help?

05:34.466 --> 05:35.676
Actually...

05:36.343 --> 05:38.846
And so, you got kicked out?

05:39.096 --> 05:40.389
That's how it is.

05:40.389 --> 05:42.057
We're seriously stuck.

05:42.057 --> 05:43.559
Is there anything you could do?

05:43.976 --> 05:46.145
Well, if you say that...

05:46.395 --> 05:47.855
Is that so?

05:48.230 --> 05:49.106
Then at least...

05:49.523 --> 05:51.108
can you make Chisa ugly?

05:51.108 --> 05:53.068
Huh? What does that
have to do with our talk?

05:53.068 --> 05:55.738
If Chisa gets hit on,
Nanaka-san is gonna be scary.

05:55.738 --> 05:57.364
Ah, that's what you mean.

05:57.364 --> 05:59.366
So what would you do if I let you in?

05:59.366 --> 06:00.326
Flirt.

06:00.409 --> 06:02.953
You're awfully true to your instincts.

06:05.581 --> 06:07.958
Okay, I'll see what I can do.

06:08.167 --> 06:09.460
Thank you.

06:09.668 --> 06:12.546
If you guys help with the setup,
I'll let you in.

06:12.546 --> 06:14.006
The stuff Kouhei is doing.

06:14.006 --> 06:15.257
- For real?
- For real?

06:15.341 --> 06:16.967
Be warned. It's gonna be tough.

06:16.967 --> 06:17.927
We'll be fine.

06:17.927 --> 06:19.845
Even Imamura can handle it, right?

06:19.845 --> 06:21.138
Then it'll be a piece of cake.

06:21.138 --> 06:22.431
I see, I see.

06:22.806 --> 06:24.767
Then follow me.

06:24.767 --> 06:26.227
- Okay!
- Okay!

06:34.068 --> 06:35.361
This is seriously heavy.

06:35.361 --> 06:36.695
Don't talk to me.

06:36.695 --> 06:38.656
Replying is exhausting.

06:38.906 --> 06:41.325
Is Imamura actually doing this?

06:41.325 --> 06:43.827
There's no way his body could...

06:53.629 --> 06:55.130
Seems like he is.

06:55.130 --> 06:57.258
- Imamura-san, how about this?
- Unbelievable.

06:57.466 --> 06:59.134
- Imamura-san!
- Everyone's looking up to him.

06:59.677 --> 07:03.347
This is the first time
I've seen him look locked in.

07:03.806 --> 07:05.558
Well, looks like we'd better get moving.

07:06.809 --> 07:08.894
Alright, let's do this boys.

07:09.061 --> 07:10.271
Okay!

07:14.149 --> 07:15.609
That guy is so cool!

07:15.609 --> 07:17.528
I know, right?

07:18.737 --> 07:21.198
Seems like the
cool, silent, handsome type.

07:21.198 --> 07:22.825
I wonder if he has a girlfriend.

07:22.825 --> 07:24.326
Let's go talk to him later.

07:25.828 --> 07:28.747
Got it? That man has betrayed us.

07:28.747 --> 07:30.124
Yeah, despose him now.

07:30.124 --> 07:31.834
Pay close attention to his face.

07:31.959 --> 07:33.210
Hold it, you guys!

07:33.210 --> 07:34.587
Huhh?

07:34.587 --> 07:36.046
Why are you stopping us, Kitahara?

07:36.046 --> 07:38.048
Are you going to forgive that shithead?

07:38.048 --> 07:40.467
Isn't this where we painfully kill him?

07:40.885 --> 07:43.137
Tsk, tsk, you're so short sighted.

07:44.096 --> 07:46.348
This is why you're all unpopular.

07:46.557 --> 07:47.975
- What did you say?
- What did you say?

07:48.267 --> 07:49.226
Listen up.

07:49.226 --> 07:51.395
Kouhei is with us.

07:51.395 --> 07:52.438
Up until just now.

07:52.438 --> 07:54.356
In a moment, he'll be our late friend.

07:54.356 --> 07:55.858
That's not what I'm saying.

07:55.941 --> 07:58.736
If we use him as bait,
won't we be able to lure those girls?

08:00.946 --> 08:01.864
What should we do?

08:01.864 --> 08:02.948
Should we try asking?

08:03.157 --> 08:06.035
Man, this is some hard work.

08:06.577 --> 08:07.995
Are you guys thirsty?

08:07.995 --> 08:09.246
Ah, now that you mention it.

08:09.246 --> 08:11.540
It's tough enough
to get you sweating after all.

08:11.540 --> 08:13.250
Huh? But you haven't done much...

08:13.250 --> 08:14.627
Don't say unnecessary things.

08:15.711 --> 08:18.589
I'd rather choose
supplementary lessons instead.

08:18.589 --> 08:21.091
OUMI FESTIVAL STAFF
ho cares about a voice actor's concert?

08:21.383 --> 08:22.801
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

08:22.801 --> 08:23.636
Times like these...

08:23.636 --> 08:26.096
really make you want an ice cold mug.

08:26.514 --> 08:28.224
Ah, I know what you mean.

08:28.224 --> 08:30.100
I want to drink too.

08:30.267 --> 08:31.268
Then, how about this?

08:31.268 --> 08:33.437
If you'd like, we can all
go drinking after this.

08:33.437 --> 08:35.856
Kind of like a
"finalized setting-up party."

08:35.856 --> 08:37.650
Eh... but...

08:37.650 --> 08:39.527
What should we do?

08:39.944 --> 08:41.529
I'll bring that guy along too.

08:41.529 --> 08:42.238
Huh?

08:44.865 --> 08:46.116
We're fine.

08:46.367 --> 08:47.368
Don't get in our way!

08:47.368 --> 08:48.786
We didn't invite you.

08:49.245 --> 08:51.747
I can't overlook my friend's happiness.

08:51.914 --> 08:53.249
That was just a mistake.

08:53.249 --> 08:55.334
We meant to say him.

08:56.001 --> 08:57.294
Oh, him?

08:57.419 --> 08:58.254
Really?

08:58.254 --> 08:59.296
Then we'll go.

08:59.421 --> 09:00.297
Yes!

09:00.881 --> 09:02.842
We'll see you after the setup's over then.

09:02.842 --> 09:04.426
Okay.

09:05.511 --> 09:06.554
Now...

09:06.554 --> 09:09.098
Bastard, showing up
at such a juicy moment.

09:09.098 --> 09:10.766
What are you doing this whole time?

09:10.975 --> 09:13.394
I was worried about you guys, of course.

09:13.394 --> 09:14.687
Then what's with that face?

09:14.687 --> 09:16.897
You get to enjoy
a women's college alone.

09:17.106 --> 09:20.568
But that doesn't matter now, does it?

09:20.776 --> 09:22.444
That's true.

09:22.444 --> 09:24.280
We finally got this chance.

09:26.657 --> 09:30.077
We have to succeed at all costs.

09:31.537 --> 09:33.998
Setup went smoothly
thanks for your help.

09:33.998 --> 09:35.958
For Kaya-sama, this is nothing.

09:37.167 --> 09:38.711
You really like her, eh?

09:39.128 --> 09:41.338
KAYA MIZUKI LIVE CONCERT
Then let me give you this.

09:41.630 --> 09:44.341
Oh, this is the...

09:44.550 --> 09:46.427
very first seat?

09:46.969 --> 09:49.847
It's rare, so it'll be nice to
watch it from a good seat.

09:51.390 --> 09:53.601
Thank you... so much...

09:53.601 --> 09:55.895
Huh? You're actually crying at this age?

09:58.147 --> 10:00.316
Good for you.

10:00.691 --> 10:01.984
Kouhei.

10:01.984 --> 10:04.486
With that ticket,
you don't need to line up.

10:04.486 --> 10:06.989
That means you can go drinking with us.

10:06.989 --> 10:08.908
W-What are you guys planning?

10:08.908 --> 10:10.868
Are you guys after my ticket?

10:10.868 --> 10:11.911
No way.

10:11.911 --> 10:14.038
We don't have any interest in it, so chill.

10:14.038 --> 10:15.956
Anyway, let's go drinking.

10:16.498 --> 10:18.417
But I have to go to the concert.

10:18.500 --> 10:21.837
It's fine, we're just drinking
in an empty classroom nearby.

10:21.837 --> 10:24.381
You can just come when it starts
and leave afterwards.

10:24.715 --> 10:26.258
You guys sure about that?

10:28.385 --> 10:29.887
Cheers.

10:30.387 --> 10:32.681
Hey, hey, what's your name?
I'm Sakurako.

10:32.681 --> 10:34.350
I'm Yuki, what school do you go to?

10:34.350 --> 10:36.519
I'm Natsumi, do you have a girlfriend?

10:39.271 --> 10:40.981
He's blushing, so cute.

10:40.981 --> 10:42.775
Hey, tell me your name.

10:44.026 --> 10:46.278
Kouhei Imamura.

10:46.487 --> 10:48.989
Oh, so you are called Kouhei-kun.

10:48.989 --> 10:51.158
You look so mature for a first-year.

10:51.158 --> 10:53.118
Hey, what do you do on your days off?

10:53.118 --> 10:55.454
Well, I...

10:55.996 --> 10:57.456
Hey, Kouhei.

10:57.581 --> 10:59.542
It's almost time.

10:59.542 --> 11:01.418
You've got a lot to prepare, don't you?

11:01.418 --> 11:03.796
Hurry up and go, you bastard.

11:03.796 --> 11:04.964
Oh, you're right.

11:05.339 --> 11:06.924
Alright, see you later.

11:06.924 --> 11:09.176
Huh? You're going already?

11:09.176 --> 11:11.387
Let's drink for a while longer.

11:11.804 --> 11:13.681
I have something important to do.

11:13.889 --> 11:15.599
No way.

11:15.599 --> 11:17.726
Why not just forget about it?

11:17.726 --> 11:21.146
Drinking with us
is definitely more fun.

11:22.189 --> 11:24.525
No, no, it'd be wrong to stop him.

11:24.525 --> 11:26.986
For him, it's actually very important.

11:27.278 --> 11:28.445
Is that so?

11:28.445 --> 11:30.030
What is it?

11:30.698 --> 11:32.950
Mizuki Kaya-sama's live concert.

11:35.327 --> 11:35.870
Huh?

11:35.870 --> 11:37.997
That's your important something?

11:37.997 --> 11:38.747
Yeah.

11:39.206 --> 11:40.332
What's with that?

11:40.332 --> 11:43.002
Forget that, stay here and drink with us.

11:43.002 --> 11:46.130
That's right,
this'll definitely be more fun.

11:46.547 --> 11:47.590
Come on now.

11:47.590 --> 11:50.217
Anime and games
are his reason for living.

11:50.217 --> 11:51.719
Just let him go.

11:52.011 --> 11:54.597
Huh? Anime and games?

11:54.597 --> 11:56.891
That's so otaku.

11:56.891 --> 11:58.726
To be honest,

11:59.018 --> 12:02.688
shouldn't you just grow up already?

12:02.980 --> 12:04.190
That's right.

12:04.190 --> 12:07.067
Kouhei-kun, you have such a nice face.

12:07.067 --> 12:08.569
What a waste.

12:08.569 --> 12:09.904
Like I care about that.

12:09.904 --> 12:12.156
To me,
this is the most important thing.

12:12.406 --> 12:13.407
"The most important"?

12:13.407 --> 12:15.075
More than drinking with us?

12:15.075 --> 12:16.619
That live concert?

12:18.287 --> 12:19.205
Huh?!

12:19.205 --> 12:20.706
What a mean thing to say!

12:20.706 --> 12:22.249
Sorry, but it's the truth.

12:22.499 --> 12:23.918
Hmph...

12:24.418 --> 12:25.419
Is that so...

12:26.795 --> 12:28.839
Then fine, you can go.

12:29.048 --> 12:29.924
Huh?

12:29.924 --> 12:31.175
I'll do just that, then.

12:31.217 --> 12:32.927
Ah, wait a second.

12:33.928 --> 12:35.221
Is there something else?

12:37.515 --> 12:39.975
You've got something on you.

12:42.895 --> 12:44.647
Well, I'm off.

12:45.189 --> 12:47.566
Yeah, goodbye.

12:47.566 --> 12:48.817
Yeah, get going.

12:48.817 --> 12:51.195
Go scream so hard
you can't catch your breath.

12:51.445 --> 12:52.947
Well, sorry about that.

12:53.656 --> 12:56.367
He's a hardcore otaku.

12:56.784 --> 12:59.662
By the way, this is the outfit
he was wearing today.

13:00.246 --> 13:01.247
Whoa, that's nuts.

13:01.413 --> 13:03.415
Is he one of those "creepy otakus?"

13:03.791 --> 13:06.627
Instead, let's talk about something else.

13:06.627 --> 13:09.547
That's right, let's forget about him.

13:14.260 --> 13:16.929
Wow, you have a rental villa?

13:16.929 --> 13:19.306
We borrowed it for our club trip.

13:19.306 --> 13:20.599
That's nice.

13:20.599 --> 13:22.726
It's much cheaper than
staying in a hotel.

13:22.726 --> 13:25.771
Being able to make
what you want sounds great, too.

13:26.146 --> 13:30.484
Then, let's all go together next time.

13:30.818 --> 13:31.819
- Freeze!
- Freeze!

13:33.279 --> 13:35.155
Ah... does that mean...

13:35.155 --> 13:37.491
you three ladies
would be going together?

13:38.534 --> 13:39.702
What are you on about?

13:39.702 --> 13:42.204
What would we do if we went by ourselves?

13:42.204 --> 13:44.707
It'd be such a waste
to stay the night like that.

13:44.707 --> 13:46.166
Let's go together.

13:48.627 --> 13:50.796
I want to try some BBQ too.

13:50.796 --> 13:53.340
Eating while watching the sunset
would be great.

13:53.340 --> 13:55.467
That sounds so fun.

13:55.968 --> 13:56.969
For real?

13:57.261 --> 13:58.387
What a...

13:59.388 --> 14:01.599
dreamlike experience!

14:03.809 --> 14:06.228
Whoops, I shouldn't get too excited.

14:06.770 --> 14:09.148
Going on vacation together sounds fun.

14:09.148 --> 14:10.774
When would be a good time to go?

14:10.774 --> 14:12.234
We need a destination too.

14:12.234 --> 14:13.527
These idiots!

14:13.944 --> 14:18.032
At the very least, I need to act like
a level-headed understanding guy.

14:18.949 --> 14:21.368
Do you want us to call up
some of our friends?

14:21.368 --> 14:23.537
It'd be better to have
equal numbers, right?

14:24.747 --> 14:25.956
I'll do anything!

14:26.707 --> 14:28.209
You're so desperate.

14:37.510 --> 14:41.055
A fairytale is whispering so low

14:41.347 --> 14:43.474
Of this false, gilded world

14:43.474 --> 14:47.144
Hiding deep within the dark

14:57.196 --> 14:58.656
Oh, right.

14:58.656 --> 14:59.698
What is it?

15:00.115 --> 15:03.369
About the beach trip,
let's invite Kouhei-kun along as well.

15:03.911 --> 15:05.788
Uhh...

15:05.788 --> 15:07.498
No, that's guy...

15:07.498 --> 15:09.792
Even if we invite him,
he might not come.

15:09.959 --> 15:11.001
Is that so?

15:11.001 --> 15:14.129
I mean, he chose the concert
over us earlier, remember?

15:14.129 --> 15:16.674
He's not interested in 3D and stuff.

15:16.674 --> 15:17.424
Hmm...

15:17.424 --> 15:19.552
Then that's all the more reason.

15:19.552 --> 15:20.386
Why?

15:20.386 --> 15:21.595
Because

15:21.595 --> 15:23.764
the fact that he suddenly left

15:23.764 --> 15:26.600
caused a lots of hassle for us, you know?

15:26.600 --> 15:27.768
That's right.

15:27.768 --> 15:29.436
His looks are really nice, too.

15:29.436 --> 15:32.231
You guys should fix him up,
even by force if necessary.

15:32.231 --> 15:34.066
That's right.

15:34.066 --> 15:35.568
What should we do?

15:35.818 --> 15:36.443
Huh?

15:37.736 --> 15:39.530
Did I just get a text?

15:39.989 --> 15:40.865
Huh?

15:40.990 --> 15:43.367
KOUHEI IMAMURAHave you seen my ticket?

15:43.868 --> 15:46.120
We'll have to use drastic measures.

15:46.120 --> 15:48.247
Like throwing away all his merch at home?

15:49.164 --> 15:50.749
I guess we have to go that far.

15:50.749 --> 15:53.377
Yeah, for example...

15:53.794 --> 15:55.588
something like this.

15:55.754 --> 15:58.340
KAYA MIZUKI LIVE CONCERT
RESERVED TICKET

15:58.507 --> 16:00.467
Is that Kouhei's?

16:00.467 --> 16:01.760
Is that his ticket?

16:01.760 --> 16:02.636
Yup, yup.

16:02.636 --> 16:04.138
When did you get it?

16:04.138 --> 16:05.598
You go Sakurako.

16:05.598 --> 16:06.765
You bet.

16:06.765 --> 16:08.976
CAN YOU TAKE A LOOK?There's no time left. Please.

16:09.810 --> 16:12.771
I was so pissed earlier that I took it.

16:13.731 --> 16:16.025
Looks like it's already paying off.

16:16.150 --> 16:19.987
He needs to grow up
and quit this kinda stuff already.

16:20.738 --> 16:23.365
Voice actors and anime, and all that.

16:23.365 --> 16:25.284
It's so unbecoming.

16:25.534 --> 16:28.537
I seriously don't get it at all.

16:29.371 --> 16:30.497
Right?

16:30.497 --> 16:31.665
Me too.

16:31.874 --> 16:34.210
Maybe he'll finally
learn something from this.

16:34.210 --> 16:36.212
This is for his sake, in a sense.

16:37.588 --> 16:39.048
I see, I see.

16:39.256 --> 16:40.966
This is what they call kindness...

16:44.386 --> 16:45.137
Huh?

16:45.638 --> 16:46.597
Huh? Wha...

16:46.597 --> 16:48.140
S-Sakurako...

16:50.518 --> 16:52.895
Alright, let's go home.

16:52.895 --> 16:53.646
Right on.

16:53.646 --> 16:54.188
Yup.

16:54.188 --> 16:55.439
W-Wait!

16:55.439 --> 16:57.441
What did you just do that for?

16:57.441 --> 16:59.401
What's with you all of a sudden?

16:59.401 --> 17:02.571
You're the ones who said he was a creep.

17:03.989 --> 17:05.407
So what?

17:05.658 --> 17:09.370
We're free to have whatever opinions
we want about his hobbies.

17:10.079 --> 17:11.080
But here's the thing.

17:11.914 --> 17:15.167
You shouldn't block something
that someone really loves.

17:17.294 --> 17:19.505
He's fine the way he is.

17:22.049 --> 17:25.594
OUMI WOMEN'S COLLEGE FESTIVAL

17:32.518 --> 17:35.771
What a waste!

17:37.314 --> 17:39.358
Our passionate summer!

17:39.567 --> 17:43.529
Breaking the curse of only
losing my virginity in my next life!

17:45.364 --> 17:47.157
All because you snapped!

17:47.157 --> 17:49.326
Then you should've done something!

17:54.748 --> 17:56.166
What are you guys doing?

17:56.542 --> 17:57.626
Right back at you.

17:59.336 --> 18:02.464
Well, you know,
there'll be another concert...

18:02.464 --> 18:03.757
It was totally amazing!

18:04.049 --> 18:07.928
Kaya-sama's concert
was beyond brilliant!

18:07.928 --> 18:08.637
Huh?

18:09.430 --> 18:11.056
You get to watch it?

18:11.056 --> 18:14.977
Yeah, the lady
in charge of setup stepped in for me.

18:15.644 --> 18:17.563
You lost your ticket?

18:17.563 --> 18:19.148
You idiot!

18:19.148 --> 18:21.609
Fine, I'll go pull some strings!

18:22.067 --> 18:24.153
How long have you been crying for?

18:24.153 --> 18:25.946
Didn't the concert end a while ago?

18:25.946 --> 18:29.700
To be that moved,
surely you must have a good seat?

18:29.700 --> 18:32.119
Ah no, it was in the very back.

18:32.578 --> 18:33.412
Huh?!

18:33.412 --> 18:36.081
Then why do you look so satisfied?

18:36.081 --> 18:38.918
I was really depressed at first.

18:39.835 --> 18:41.378
But when the concert started,

18:44.048 --> 18:46.425
it all blew away!

18:50.387 --> 18:52.806
You really are a creep!

18:52.806 --> 18:53.307
Indeed.

18:53.307 --> 18:57.061
Shut up, how could you guys not
understand Kaya-sama's majesty!

18:57.061 --> 18:57.770
Like I care.

18:57.770 --> 18:59.522
Whatever, let's go drinking.

18:59.522 --> 19:00.856
It's Imamura's treat.

19:00.856 --> 19:01.899
Why me?

19:01.899 --> 19:04.276
A consolation party for
trying to win the girls.

19:06.237 --> 19:08.614
Uh... Chisa-san.

19:08.614 --> 19:09.406
What?

19:09.657 --> 19:12.076
You managed to avoid
unwanted flirting, right?

19:12.076 --> 19:13.452
You could say that.

19:14.036 --> 19:15.538
Then why...

19:15.746 --> 19:17.414
are you so angry?

19:20.125 --> 19:22.336
After that, Azusa-san came in.

19:22.795 --> 19:25.214
You must have been hit on
by a lot of people.

19:25.339 --> 19:26.715
Well...

19:26.715 --> 19:28.717
Ah, about that.

19:28.717 --> 19:29.426
This girl...

19:29.802 --> 19:32.930
has such a boyfriend.
That flirting doesn't work on her.

19:33.347 --> 19:34.932
Heh!?

19:36.350 --> 19:37.726
Excuse me.

19:38.727 --> 19:39.311
Hm?

19:42.106 --> 19:43.858
We don't see you around often.

19:43.858 --> 19:45.734
Are you here to learn about diving?

19:45.818 --> 19:47.570
Ah no, not for that.

19:47.778 --> 19:50.197
My sister wanted me
to hand this to Kouhei-kun.

19:50.197 --> 19:52.449
Hnah? For me?

19:52.449 --> 19:56.078
KOUHEI IMAMURA-KUN

19:57.788 --> 19:59.707
She said you can have this, if you'd like.

19:59.915 --> 20:00.541
Huh?

20:00.749 --> 20:02.167
Oh, this is...

20:02.167 --> 20:03.627
This name looks familiar.

20:04.086 --> 20:07.381
I think the one who attended the concert
also had this name.

20:07.381 --> 20:08.299
Exactly.

20:10.217 --> 20:13.220
My big sister is a voice actress.

20:13.470 --> 20:16.557
Does that mean the person
with the cakey makeup...

20:17.016 --> 20:19.018
That's right, she's Kaya Mizuki-san.

20:19.226 --> 20:20.811
I told you I'd let you meet her.

20:29.236 --> 20:30.654
W-What's wrong?

20:30.654 --> 20:32.198
Don't mind him.

20:32.198 --> 20:34.909
He's taking in the joy
of meeting her while regretting

20:34.909 --> 20:36.327
of not talking to her at all.

20:36.327 --> 20:39.496
Why!?
Why didn't you tell me beforehand!?

20:39.496 --> 20:40.789
How could I?

20:41.207 --> 20:43.667
If we told you then
you wouldn't have worked.

20:43.834 --> 20:44.877
No doubt about it.

20:45.544 --> 20:48.505
My sister was very happy
to see you cheering her on.

20:49.381 --> 20:51.800
She even praised Iori.

20:52.468 --> 20:53.135
Huh?

20:53.385 --> 20:54.178
Me?

20:55.137 --> 20:56.430
What did you do?

20:56.430 --> 20:58.891
I can't remember doing anything.

20:59.475 --> 21:01.936
KAYA MIZUKI-SAMA

21:02.228 --> 21:05.314
That cross-dressing was pretty cute.

21:05.314 --> 21:07.191
You mean Iori and Kouhei?

21:07.191 --> 21:09.026
I laughed so hard.

21:09.568 --> 21:10.945
That's right, Azusa.

21:11.111 --> 21:12.655
Speaking of Iori.

21:12.655 --> 21:13.447
Huh?

21:13.656 --> 21:17.159
I understand why you praised him now.

21:17.159 --> 21:18.619
Did something happen?

21:18.619 --> 21:19.370
Yeah.

21:20.371 --> 21:21.497
Just something.

21:22.206 --> 21:22.665
CAKIE CAFE

21:22.665 --> 21:25.251
He's a genuine creep.

21:26.085 --> 21:30.464
Maybe everyone's interests
just seem like that to other people.

21:30.881 --> 21:32.007
That might be it.

21:32.174 --> 21:34.426
But that's exactly what makes me think...

21:37.471 --> 21:40.307
he's really an amazing guy.

21:41.517 --> 21:43.727
But you just called him a creep.

21:43.727 --> 21:45.145
That's exactly why.

21:45.145 --> 21:45.938
Huh?

21:46.272 --> 21:48.816
Because even after being told that,

21:48.816 --> 21:51.527
he still refuses to give up
the things he loves.

21:53.195 --> 21:55.698
Isn't that amazing?

21:57.616 --> 22:01.203
Even if nobody gets your hobbies...

22:02.037 --> 22:05.708
To be accepted for who you are,
even if you're a bit crazy about it...

22:11.547 --> 22:12.715
That's true happiness.

22:21.599 --> 22:23.184
Wanna talk to you, wanna talk to you

22:23.184 --> 22:25.019
First I gotta know all about you,
isn't that right?

22:25.019 --> 22:26.979
Ending it off at round one
reeks of boredom

22:26.979 --> 22:28.731
Rounds two, three, and four is the plan

22:28.731 --> 22:30.441
As the night gets deeper,
true thoughts escape

22:30.441 --> 22:32.359
Let us go on and on and dive down late

22:32.359 --> 22:35.404
Your history, your scenery, for me
will your pages get slippery

22:35.404 --> 22:37.448
Hey, show me even more

22:37.448 --> 22:39.158
This is my track and you are
the featured guest

22:39.158 --> 22:40.784
We'll forget by the time when the dawn hits

22:40.784 --> 22:42.244
Being incomplete is perfection

22:42.244 --> 22:44.496
Hey, show me even more

22:44.496 --> 22:46.040
My mouth keeps slipping,
my mouth keeps slipping

22:46.040 --> 22:47.666
Complaint whether we sober upward

22:47.666 --> 22:49.710
For now, let's ride high on this feeling

22:50.127 --> 22:56.175
Let's live this moment with all we can
without leaving a single regret,

22:56.675 --> 22:58.385
We are gonna do it,
we go past the limit now

22:58.385 --> 22:59.970
Not just the whole night,
party till the sun is out

22:59.970 --> 23:02.139
Let's fly high

23:02.139 --> 23:02.765
(Let's fly high)

23:02.765 --> 23:04.767
So first, you just strip it down

23:04.767 --> 23:07.019
An exposed and feral kind of bond

23:07.019 --> 23:10.648
It's the way of life's cycle,
let us go way beyond

23:10.648 --> 23:12.316
The very moment that we met
I drop my shy act

23:12.316 --> 23:14.068
I wanna bare it all
and say what I need to say

23:14.068 --> 23:16.028
Do it now...

23:16.820 --> 23:21.116
This is the magic spell that breaks
down each and every single wall

23:21.116 --> 23:24.578
And once you get used to it,
you won't feel a thing at all

23:24.578 --> 23:26.080
Being without clothes is
a mystery I live in

23:26.080 --> 23:27.873
The drinking and chatting
is flowing more freely

23:27.873 --> 23:30.209
Try it now...

23:30.668 --> 23:34.129
And right before you realize
what's going on

23:34.129 --> 23:38.384
Your heart will catch right up
and finally be free

23:44.932 --> 23:49.937
NEXT TIME: THE CHARPY IMPACT TEST
